# Force LF on checkout regardless of a checkout tool's local core.autocrlf.
# Without this, Git for Windows (autocrlf=true on GitHub's Windows runners)
# writes CRLF for every text file at checkout time, while MSYS2's own git --
# a separate install, used by every workflow step once setup-msys2 runs --
# compares those bytes under its own autocrlf policy and reports nearly the
# whole tree as modified. eol=lf pins the checked-out line ending so both
# gits agree without either one's autocrlf setting mattering.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A verbatim upstream fixture (Pascal community sources are commonly CRLF);
# keep it byte-for-byte rather than renormalize it.
examples/languages/pl0/samples/gcd.pas -text
